  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0 (branch cut from upstream/main f490458a82c45bcf8ba44e8258a77b3cf5b31397).\n\n## What reproduced, and what did not\n\nI loaded the user's `cutouts.camproj` (attachment to #241) through the project API on upstream/main f490458a. For Face, Trace, 2D Contour and 2D Pocket I created an op with the GUI's default parameters and gave it each of these picks: the planar top face, all 57 edge chains rimming it, the outer rim's 4 chains, one cutout's 9 chains, and the whole model as the source.\n\n**Already fixed on main (pinned there):**\n- Picking the face and the edges resolves: 1 outer ring and 6 hole rings.\n- Facing on the face pick used to refuse with \"15.15 mm gap / 3 mm tool\". That was #260, fixed by PR #313 (merge `1da9695b`) and shipped in v0.15.0. It is pinned by `face_concave_holes` in camcraft-motion. Face on the face pick now generates 726 moves on main.\n- Trace, 2D Contour and 2D Pocket on the face pick and on the edge picks generated on main.\n\n**Still failing on main, fixed here (all three were wrong refusals on a valid closed part):**\n1. **Face on the edge picks refused**: \"two holes stand 0.63 mm apart on the row at Y=-25.50\". A chain-only Face pick is clipped by the part's silhouette. That silhouette came from the fallback (see 2), which unions the facet shadows through `Region::new`'s nesting parity. Any bottom-face facet whose shadow lay inside a top-face facet's shadow became a hole, so 27 phantom triangles (up to 433 mm²) were cut into the solid webs. The fallback is now a pure union (`Region::union_all`, each shadow oriented CCW).\n2. **The slicer refused the closed mesh**: \"open at z = -19.375: 12 dangling chord ends\". The part's shared corners scatter by up to 1.04 µm, and the slicer's 1 µm rounded weld key split crossing pairs that straddled a rounding boundary. The slicer keeps the exact key as its first try. Only when that leaves ends dangling does it re-slice with chord ends welded within 2 µm through a neighbourhood search, in the new `camcraft_geometry::geometry::slice_weld`. Every mesh that sliced before slices exactly as before. A real 0.1 mm gap is still refused as open. A first version used the tolerance weld for every slice; the gate caught it moving an exact mesh's islands (`blind_floor` Crossing), so it is a fallback only (second commit). This also fixes Face with the whole model as its source, which refused with the same \"open mesh\" error.\n3. **Contour and Trace with the whole model as source refused** with \"no material at z = 0.000\". The part's top corners are uneven by 3e-13 mm, and a section exactly at Top of Part met only the highest corner. `section` now retries 1 µm lower on an empty answer, as it already did on an error. A plane that really misses the part still refuses, and the message now says what to change: \"the source spans Z0.000 to Z5.000; set Top of Part Z inside that span, or pick the face or edges to machine\".\n\nAfter the fix, every pick set above generates on the user's project for all four kinds with no verifier warnings. Face on edge picks produces the same 726-move path as Face on the face pick.\n\n**Not part of this fix:** the issue's aside asks for box selection of edges. That is a new UI feature, filed as #979.\n\n## Changed\n- `crates/geometry/src/geometry/slice_weld.rs` (new): the exact weld plus a tolerance weld (spatial hash over neighbouring cells). `slice.rs` tries exact, then tolerant on `Open`.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/picks.rs`: `silhouette`'s fallback is `facet_shadow`, a pure union.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/material.rs`: `section` retries on empty, and the empty refusal names the Z span.\n- `docs/decisions/241-cutouts-ops.md`: the reproduction and the decisions.\n\n## Tests (each fails on the old code; checked by reverting the fix file and rerunning)\n- `an_open_mesh_rim_pick_faces_the_whole_top_with_no_phantom_holes` (camcraft-app `face_holes`): an open plate with nested bottom facets, rim chains picked. The region is one 1600 mm² loop, and the path equals the face pick's path.\n- `sub_micrometre_corner_scatter_still_welds_into_a_closed_slice` and `a_tenth_of_a_millimetre_gap_is_still_open` (camcraft-geometry `slice`). The second one passes on the old code too; it is the control that the tolerance stays at micrometre scale.\n- `a_whole_model_contour_at_a_noisy_top_sections_the_part` and `a_top_plane_above_the_part_still_refuses_and_names_the_span` (camcraft-app `top_plane_noise`, new). The contour stays a tool radius off the box and has no warnings.\n\nThe user's project itself is not committed: it is 697 KB and the user's file. The synthetic fixtures reproduce each mechanism.\n\n## Gate\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` fell back to the batch plan because camcraft-geometry changed. It ran geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app and ui suites plus clippy `-D warnings` across all of them: **green** on the final head 45373c9b (9 steps, 15.1 min). The first run, on 7132909e, was red on `blind_floor` (see item 2) and led to the fallback-only weld.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The GUI itself: no viewport clicks. The picks were driven through `SetOperationGeometry`, which is the command the clicks use.\n- Release-tier heavy lanes and the snapshot PNGs. No PNG was changed.\n- Goldens: none moved (`golden_cl` and `solid_law_goldens` pass unchanged).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Facing, Trace and 2D Contour work on imported parts whose corners carry float noise: edge picks no longer refuse on phantom holes, a closed mesh no longer slices as \"open\", and a whole-model contour at Top of Part no longer reads \"no material\" (#241)\n\nFixes #241\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
